<surname>Hohmann</surname><given-names>HP</given-names></name><name><surname>Remy</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheidereit</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>van Loon</surname><given-names>APGM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Maintenance of NF-<italic>&#x003ba;</italic>B activity is dependent on protein synthesis and the continuous presence of external stimuli</article-title><source>Mol Cell Biol</source><year>1991</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>259</fpage><lpage>266</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Mol Cell Biol||11|259||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1986224</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jackman</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Calvert</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Folate-based thymidylate synthase inhibitors as anticancer drugs</article-title><source>Ann Oncol</source><year>1995</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>871</fpage><lpage>881</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Ann Oncol||6|871||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8624289</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jackman</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kelland</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimbell</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gibson</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Aherne</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Hardcastle</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyle</surname><given-names>FT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanisms of acquired resistance to the quinazoline thymidylate synthase inhibitor ZD1694 (Tomudex) in one mouse and three human cell lines</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>1995</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>914</fpage><lpage>924</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||71|914||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7537518</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How NF-kappaB is activated: the role of the IkappaB kinase (IKK) complex</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>1999</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>6867</fpage><lpage>6874</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Oncogene||18|6867||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10602462</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krappmann</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Emmerich</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kordes</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Scharschmidt</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Dorken</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheidereit</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular mechanisms of constitutive NF-kappaB&#x0002f;Rel activation in Hodgkin&#x0002f;Reed&#x02013;Sternberg cells</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>1999</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>943</fpage><lpage>953</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Oncogene||18|943||bib16|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10023670</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pahl</surname><given-names>HL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Activators and target genes of Rel&#x0002f;NF-kappaB transcription factors</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>1999</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>6853</fpage><lpage>6866</lpag